<p>Compare with 6.A, which called <code>resp.sendError(404, "No device with this id")</code> and showed Tomcat's error page. Here the controller throws; <code>BasicErrorController</code> looks for <code>templates/error/404.html</code> (then <code>error/4xx.html</code>, then <code>error.html</code>) and passes it <code>status</code>, <code>error</code> and <code>path</code>. The exception message is <em>not</em> passed by default (<code>server.error.include-message</code> is <code>never</code>), which is safer — internal details stay on the server.</p>
