<p>Method security works through a proxy around the bean, exactly like <code>@Transactional</code> in CS.3, so it shares its blind spots. Exercise 2 measures them: a call to <code>this.adminReport()</code> inside the same class runs for a student (200), an object made with <code>new</code> runs for a student (200), and <code>hasAuthority('ADMIN')</code> refuses the admin (403) because the authority is <code>ROLE_ADMIN</code>. Forgetting <code>@EnableMethodSecurity</code> has the same effect as the <code>new</code> case: no proxy, the annotation is silently ignored.</p>
